title: Fibershed
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
url: https://fibershed.org/

The region that could clothe you: the farms, mills, dyers, and makers close enough to make your clothes from soil to skin.

The idea comes from [[Rebecca Burgess]]. In 2011 she set out to wear only clothes grown, woven, and sewn in her part of North Central California. Finding the people who could do that is what drew the map.

The nonprofit Fibershed followed in 2013. Its [[history page|https://fibershed.org/history/]] credits her project with introducing the concept.

A [[material shed|Materialshed]] widens it from fiber to everything a thing is made of.

See [[BioRegion]].
